{title: Wash And Be Clean}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 5:1–3; 5:9–12; 5:13–14; 5:15–17; Luke 4:27}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Naaman stood in [C]power and pride
Com[Dm]mander of Aram's army wide
Through him [C]the Lord gave victory
[Bb]But leprosy [C]marked his body
[Dm]A young girl from Israel's land
Served [C/D]in Naaman's [Dm]wife's hand
She [C]spoke of a prophet in Samaria
[Bb]Who could heal his [C]skin so [Dm]badly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Go wash seven times [C]in the Jordan
[Bb]Let your flesh be [C]clean and restored
The [Dm]simple word is [C]God's way
[Bb]Grace that cannot be [C]bought or [Dm]paid
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He came with hors[C]es and chariots
[Bb]To the door of [C]Elisha's house
[Dm]But the prophet [C]sent a messenger
[Bb]With words that [C]made Naaman frown
[Dm]He thought the [C]man would come [Dm]out
Wave his hand and cure the [Bb]doubt
Instead he was [C]told to dip
In [Bb]waters he deemed too [C]small to [Dm]fix
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
His servants [C]spoke with gentle care
[Bb]Why did you turn [C]away in rage
[Dm]If the prophet [C]asked for greatness
[Bb]Would you not have [C]done his bidding
[Dm]So he [C]went down to the [Dm]river
Dipped himself seven times in the [Bb]water
His flesh was like a [C]young boy's skin
[Bb]He was clean and he [C]came back [Dm]in
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Now I know there [C]is no God in all [Bb]the earth
Except in [C]Israel's land
[Dm]So please ac[C]cept a gift from your [Bb]servant
For I have found [C]the promise and the [Dm]plan
But Elis[C]ha refused the [Dm]silver
Saying I will ac[Bb]cept nothing
Naaman [C]asked for earth to [Bb]carry
So he could [C]serve the Lord for[Dm]ever
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Only [C]Naaman the [Bb]Syrian was [C]cleansed
While [Dm]many [C]lepers went un[Bb]healed
Grace found the [C]outsider in the [Dm]end
{end_of_verse}
